        <mxCell id="2. 67" value="topics" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;fontSize=11;startArrow=block;startFill=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#BD7000;fontColor=#BD7000;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="2. 41" target="2. 48">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2. 68" value="topics" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;fontSize=11;startArrow=block;startFill=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#BD7000;fontColor=#BD7000;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="2. 42" target="2. 49">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2. 69" value="topics" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;fontSize=11;startArrow=block;startFill=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#BD7000;fontColor=#BD7000;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="2. 43" target="2. 50">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2. 70" value="topics" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;fontSize=11;startArrow=block;startFill=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#BD7000;fontColor=#BD7000;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="2. 44" target="2. 51">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2. 71" value="topics" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;fontSize=11;startArrow=block;startFill=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#BD7000;fontColor=#BD7000;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.3;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="2. 45" target="2. 59">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2. 72" value="set/watchdog_trigger (Wi-Fi)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;fontSize=11;startArrow=block;startFill=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#BD7000;fontColor=#BD7000;fontStyle=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.75;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="2. 38" target="2. 59">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="960" y="916" />
              <mxPoint x="960" y="1481" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2. 73" value="&lt;b&gt;One loop, one fate.&lt;/b&gt; Every server of the G1 is stepped in the same RobotDriverROS loop. Any exception (watchdog lost, a second commanding client, a driver error) ends control_loop(), and ~RobotDriverROS() deinitializes the robot: arms released, Move(0, 0, 0), the robot keeps standing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;unitree_drivers locks internally, so threads would be possible; the single loop is chosen because the whole robot then always stops together." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1550" width="620" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2. 74" value="&lt;b&gt;Exclusive topics (enforced by SAS).&lt;/b&gt; set/target_joint_*, set/watchdog_trigger and the legged set/ topics accept a single publisher; a second one makes the server callback throw, which stops the driver.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kinematic controller = the only commanding client (blacklist WATCHDOG_CONTROL).&lt;br&gt;Watchdog node = the only watchdog client (blacklist JOINT_CONTROL).&lt;br&gt;Monitors (RViz, loggers) blacklist both." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="680" y="1550" width="620" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2. 75" value="&lt;b&gt;Watchdog over Wi-Fi.&lt;/b&gt; Only the main prefix has an active watchdog (no client triggers the limb prefixes). If Wi-Fi fails, triggers stop arriving and the robot stops.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SAS also checks the trigger delay, so the desktop and robot clocks must be in sync (chrony / NTP).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The onboard twist timeout covers a crashed or stalled kinematic controller." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1330" y="1550" width="620" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="3. Topic standard" id="legged-arch-3">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2200" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="3. 1" value="&lt;b&gt;Proposed topic standard for legged robots&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every LeggedRobotDriver exposes exactly these topics under its prefix (e.g. &lt;code&gt;sas_g1/g1_1&lt;/code&gt;). The client flag is the SAS MODE_BLACKLIST_FLAG that creates the topic on the client side; blacklisting it removes the topic. &quot;Single publisher&quot; topics are enforced by the server: a second publisher stops the driver. Robot-specific extras (e.g. B1 battery) may be added by extra_control_loop_step(), but a generic client never depends on them." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="10" width="1650" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3. 2" value="&lt;table style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;width:100%'&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Topic&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Type&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Direction&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Client flag&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Single publisher&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#eeeeee;font-weight:bold' colspan='6'&gt;Base topics under &amp;lt;prefix&amp;gt;/ (the base has no joints: its SAS joint topics are empty)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;set/watchdog_trigger&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;sas_msgs/WatchdogTrigger&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;client → server&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;WATCHDOG_CONTROL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Sent by the watchdog node (desktop). A failure stops the whole driver.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;set/shutdown&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;sas_msgs/Bool&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;client → server&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;any client&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Stops the whole driver.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;get/info&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;sas_legged_msgs/LeggedRobotInfo&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;server → client&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_MONITORING&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Limbs and their joint names, supported modes and functionalities, orientation limits. transient_local, published once.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;get/status&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;sas_legged_msgs/LeggedRobotStatus&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;server → client&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_MONITORING&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Current mode, accepts_* flags, and commandable_limbs (which limbs accept targets now).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;get/imu&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;sensor_msgs/Imu&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;server → client&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_MONITORING&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Base orientation, angular velocity, linear acceleration (with gravity), body frame.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;set/high_level_mode&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;sas_legged_msgs/HighLevelMode&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;client → server&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_CONTROL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;IDLE / STANDING / WALKING (rules in the table below). Unsupported modes are rejected and logged.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;set/target_twist&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;geometry_msgs/TwistStamped&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;client → server&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_CONTROL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Body frame. Zero velocity is sent if no message arrives within twist_timeout_sec.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;set/target_base_height&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;std_msgs/Float64&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;client → server&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_CONTROL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Meters. Only if supports_base_height.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;set/target_base_orientation&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;geometry_msgs/QuaternionStamped&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;client → server&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_CONTROL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Only if supports_base_orientation.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#eeeeee;font-weight:bold' colspan='6'&gt;Limb topics under &amp;lt;prefix&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;name&amp;gt;/ (existing SAS, one RobotDriverServer per limb)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;get/joint_states&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;sensor_msgs/JointState&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;server → client&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_MONITORING&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Joints of the limb. Every joint of the robot belongs to exactly one limb. Order = get/info limbs[i].joint_names.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;get/joint_positions_min | max&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;std_msgs/Float64MultiArray&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;server → client&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_MONITORING&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Joint limits of the limb.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;set/target_joint_positions&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;std_msgs/Float64MultiArray&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;client → server&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_CONTROL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Applied only while the limb is commandable (get/status commandable_limbs).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;set/target_joint_velocities | forces&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;std_msgs/Float64MultiArray&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;client → server&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_CONTROL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Optional, same rule.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;code&gt;set/shutdown&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;sas_msgs/Bool&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;client → server&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;any client&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Stops the whole driver. No client triggers the limb watchdogs; the base watchdog stops everything.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="100" width="1650" height="470" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3. 3" value="&lt;b&gt;Client roles&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="600" width="400" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3. 4" value="&lt;table style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px'&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Node&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Runs on&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Blacklist&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Can&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Kinematic controller&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;onboard computer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;WATCHDOG_CONTROL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;command + monitor (the only commanding client)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Watchdog node&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;desktop computer&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_CONTROL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;watchdog + monitor (the only watchdog client)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Monitors (RViz, loggers)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;anywhere&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;JOINT_CONTROL, WATCHDOG_CONTROL&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;monitor only (any number)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="630" width="1000" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3. 5" value="&lt;b&gt;High-level modes&lt;/b&gt; (applied by LeggedRobotDriverROS; get/status reports what is accepted now)" style="text;html=1;align=left;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="600" width="700" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3. 6" value="&lt;table style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px'&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Mode&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;set/target_twist&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;set/target_base_orientation&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;set/target_base_height&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Limb targets&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style='border:1px solid #999;padding:4px 6px;background:#60a917;color:#fff;text-align:left'&gt;Robot&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;b&gt;IDLE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;ignored (zero velocity sent)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;ignored&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;ignored&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;ignored, the limbs hold still&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;On and balancing. Never damping or lying down (it could fall).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;b&gt;STANDING&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;ignored (zero velocity sent)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;accepted, if supported&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;accepted, if supported&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;accepted by the commandable limbs&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Cannot walk.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;&lt;b&gt;WALKING&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;accepted&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;ignored&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;accepted, if supported&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;accepted by the commandable limbs (e.g. H1 arms yes, G1 arms no)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style='border:1px solid #bbb;padding:4px 6px;vertical-align:top'&gt;Walks.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p style='font-size:12px;margin-top:6px'&gt;The driver starts in &lt;b&gt;IDLE&lt;/b&gt;. Each driver manages its own mode changes in set_high_level_mode() (e.g. stopping before WALKING to STANDING); the standard only fixes what each mode accepts.&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="630" width="1050" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
